   INDUSTRIAL AND COMMERCIAL MARINGA, PARANA, BRAZIL},
Journal = {ROSA DOS VENTOS-TURISMO E HOSPITALIDADE},
Year = {2016},
Volume = {8},
Number = {2},
Pages = {124-135},
Month = {APR-JUN},
Abstract = {This paper presents the results of a survey on the profile of the 41g of
   the Agriculture and Stockbreeding, Industrial and Commercial Exhibition
   Fair of Maringa {[}Expoinga]. The opinion of participants about the
   event, services and used urban infrastructure was considered. The demand
   of the fair, represented by tourists, excursionists and local community
   was characterized from the endogenous and exogenous variables.
   Therefore, we applied a questionnaire with a sample of 1,420 visitors
   during the 41st edition, in the period 10-20 May 2013. The questionnaire
   consisted of 22 structured questions was applied to the exhibition
   visitors at the gates of out of the park, so that they could say in his
   stay at the event. Respondents were divided into three types classified
   according to the origin of their homes and the time spent in the city of
   Maringa. The results indicate a mostly local audience with relatively
   low education and who seek event for leisure. The data can enable agents
   organizers of the event direct guidelines to make the experience more
   satisfying event for participants and more lucrative for investors.},
